XY(r) = 38 + \sqrt{324 - r^2} - \sqrt{400 - r^2}
\]
for \(r \in (0, 18]\). This function is continuous and decreasing, with range \((38 - 2\sqrt{19},\; 36) \approx (29.28,\; 36)\). Since \(r\) must be nonzero, \(XY\) can approach \(36\) arbitrarily closely but cannot equal \(36\). All integers from \(30\) to \(35\) are achievable, with \(35\) being the largest.

